-- T6 sentinel: TODAY is INDEPENDENT of the valid-time axis.
--
-- Update (option (b), 2026-07-08): tcValidTime is no longer fully latent —
-- `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` now reads it as a fallback (crValidTime is a real
-- CtxReads field with an instrumented reader). But TODAY still reads only
-- tcSystemTime, so `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` remains value-transparent for the
-- TODAY-based thunks below and must NOT perturb their caching. This golden
-- now LOCKS that independence (the valid-time→law-version flow is exercised
-- by temporal-rule-version-validtime.l4 instead). Values are unchanged.
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z;
-- serial(2025-01-31) = 739646.

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

-- expected: 5 (override transparent for context-free values)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000)) (2 PLUS 3)

`shared today V` MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY

-- expected: 739646 — the shared thunk is forced (and cached) while
-- tcValidTime is overridden to 2000-01-01; TODAY correctly ignores it
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000)) `shared today V`

-- expected: 739646 — the cache remains valid at ambient (no read axis
-- differs), so this also guards against over-invalidation
#EVAL `shared today V`

-- expected: 739646 (control)
#EVAL DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2025)
